import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs title="Control Flow" description="Conditionals and loops in RUDRA: if, while, for, break and continue." slug="control-flow">
  <p class="lead">RUDRA provides conditional branching and loops with a familiar shape.</p>

  <h2>Conditionals</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={`fn main() {
    let n = 7;
    if n > 10 {
        print("big");
    } else if n > 5 {
        print("medium");
    } else {
        print("small");
    }
}`} />

  <h2>While loops</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={`fn main() {
    let mut i = 0;
    let mut total = 0;
    while i < 5 {
        total = total + i;
        i = i + 1;
    }
    print(total);
}`} />
  <p>This program prints <code>10</code>.</p>

  <h2>For loops over a range</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={`fn main() {
    for k in 0..3 {
        print(k);
    }
}`} />
  <p>The range <code>0..3</code> yields <code>0</code>, <code>1</code> and <code>2</code>.</p>

  <h2>Operators</h2>
  <p>Arithmetic: <code>+ - * / %</code>. Comparison: <code>== != &lt; &gt; &lt;= &gt;=</code>. Logical: <code>&amp;&amp; || !</code>.</p>
</Docs>
